# playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
Connect the CTA / “Schedule a Demo” form on this page only to Formspree (or Getform) so submissions are stored and emailed. Do not change any other forms or pages.

## Behavior
- On submit, send the form data (name, email, phone, and any other existing fields) to a Formspree (or Getform) endpoint.
- Show a clear success message after a successful submit.
- Show a simple error message if the request fails.
- Keep client-side validation for required fields (name, email).
- Disable the submit button while the request is in progress.

## Setup notes
- Use an environment variable for the Formspree/Getform endpoint (e.g. NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT or similar).
- Do not hardcode the form ID in a way that can’t be changed easily.
- Formspree/Getform will handle storing the lead and sending the email notification — no extra email service needed in this task.

## Constraints
- Only wire up the existing CTA form on this page.
- Do not alter layout, styling, or other sections.
- Keep the current field names and labels.
- Works with the existing React/Next.js form component.

## Deliverables
- Updated form submit handler that POSTs to the Formspree/Getform endpoint.
- Success and error states in the UI.
- Short comment or README note on which env variable to set.

Implement lead capture for this page’s CTA form only via Formspree or Getform.